## Run MOJ forms locally via Docker

### Goals

Group containers into functional networks:

- `app-net` — app + api + workers + metadata + token cache
- `db-net` — Postgres/Redis, shared only with the services that need them

Expose only the ports your host actually needs (usually zero for internal services).

Prevent containers from accessing services they shouldn't.

## Repositories involved

The following repositories may need changes during this process:

- `fb-user-datastore`
- `fb-editor`
- `fb-metadata-api`
- `fb-submitter`
- the services in `fb-runner` (note: `fb-runner` does not have its own database)
- `hmcts-complaints-formbuilder-adapter`

